From: yzddmr6 <46088090+yzddmr6@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_battmgr: take the erhai v0.7.2 driver

Replace drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c with the file of erhai tag
erhai-v0.7.2 (linux-sm8750-erhai) and add its erhai_otg_glink.h. The erhai
history of this file passes through a v7.2.10 merge and a repair of tails
lost in it (67cdfbca6), so its commits do not replay on Linux 7.2.15 one by
one; the final file is taken as a whole instead. It builds on 7.2.15
without other erhai changes.

For oneplus,pad2pro-pmic-glink this brings, among others:
 - battery readings: current sign as the class expects, no POWER_NOW
 - no SM8550 charge-control opcode 0x48 or properties 25/26 (vendor
   commands in this firmware); thresholds enforced with property 24
 - USB VBUS for sinks (OTG boost driven by the firmware notifications)
 - fixed 9 V PD request when UCSI reports a PD sink and the source offers
   a 9 V fixed PDO; USB type from USB_ADAP_TYPE
 - charger notifications no longer wake the system
 - the hooks the erhai PPS driver registers with (erhai_pps_register).
   That driver (CHARGER_ERHAI_PPS) and SC8547A are not built here, so no
   PPS is negotiated.

It also replaces the battery manager changes of the Armada series on this
file (0503 battery name, 0901 charge unit, 0902 charge now, 0903 charge
current limit, 0904 threshold set failures): the erhai file sets the unit
to mAh and reports CHARGE_NOW itself; constant_charge_current and
constant_charge_current_max are no longer exported (nothing on this system
uses them). The battery is named "qcom-battmgr-bat" again.

